---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import AiLandingHero from '../../components/AiLandingHero.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import { describeServiceHref } from '../../data/contact';

const context = 'AI-assisted service design';
---

<Base
  title="AI-assisted public service design | Registry Stack"
  description="Use research and service requirements to design a government service. Try a prototype with staff and applicants, then give your delivery team a clear brief."
  ogImagePath="/og-ai.png"
  ogImageAlt="Registry Stack: Design, adapt and access public services with AI."
>
  <SiteHeader current="ai-service-design" />
  <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1">
    <AiLandingHero
      eyebrow="AI-assisted service design"
      heading="Design a service you can test before you build."
      lead="Turn research and service requirements into a brief with AI. Test a prototype with applicants and staff before you decide what to build."
      context={context}
      exampleHref="#worked-example"
      exampleLabel="See the enrolment example"
      exampleNote="Fictional example: a delivery partner’s draft enrolment brief identifies an age check and a rule the education authority must confirm."
      note="Available as a scoped engagement, mainly through our partners."
    >
      <p class="ai-example-label">Example: brief prepared by your delivery partner</p>
      <p class="ai-example-title">School enrolment</p>
      <dl class="ai-example-rows">
        <div><dt>Form item 1</dt><dd>The parent supplies the child’s date of birth.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Proposed change</dt><dd>Ask the civil register if the child meets the age rule.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Decision for the education authority</dt><dd>Which cut-off date applies to this school year?</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </AiLandingHero>

    <section class="section section-muted" id="worked-example" aria-labelledby="example-title">
      <div class="section-inner approach-split">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">Example: school enrolment</p>
          <h2 id="example-title">Help a parent apply for school</h2>
          <p>A parent brings a form to the school office. The officer enters the child’s date of birth and confirms it with the parent.</p>
          <p>The team tries a prototype that asks an approved civil register for an age check. If the source can’t answer, the screen prompts the officer to review the document with the parent.</p>
          <p>The education authority confirms the age rule. The civil-registration authority decides whether it can offer the check and what information it can return.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="editorial-callout">
          <h3>Three situations to test</h3>
          <ol class="approach-steps">
            <li><strong>The child qualifies for the local school</strong><span>Confirm the assignment and give the parent a reference.</span></li>
            <li><strong>The source can’t confirm the child’s age</strong><span>Guide the officer through the agreed manual check.</span></li>
            <li><strong>The parent requests another school</strong><span>Record the district officer’s decision. An authorized person or service applies it to the register.</span></li>
          </ol>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="outputs-title">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <h2 id="outputs-title">Give your delivery team a brief they can build from</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="value-grid">
          <article>
            <h3>See where people need help</h3>
            <p>Work through the planned service with staff and applicants. Keep source references and, when adapting an existing form, its item numbers so everyone can check each proposed change.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h3>Resolve the questions that affect the build</h3>
            <p>Use AI to organize the evidence and flag gaps. Ask the responsible teams to confirm which rules apply, which sources can be used and who can decide an exception.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h3>Find problems in a prototype</h3>
            <p>Ask applicants and staff to try common and difficult cases. Use what you learn to revise the brief and agree what to test in the working service.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <p class="section-note">We offer this design method as a scoped engagement, delivered mainly through our partners. The brief guides <a href="/customization/">how we use AI in implementation</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="final-cta" aria-labelledby="next-title">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <h2 id="next-title">Discuss the service you need to design</h2>
        <p>Bring the requirements for a new service, or a form and process you want to adapt. We run service design with our partners, and the brief guides a scoped implementation.</p>
        <div class="section-links">
          <a class="button button-primary" href={describeServiceHref(context)} data-journey="service-inquiry">Discuss your service</a>
          <a class="button button-secondary" href="/pricing/#process">See how implementation works</a>
        </div>
        <p class="final-cta-note"><a href="/pricing/">View implementation and support options</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</Base>
